This project is the on-car (native QNX) layer of a two-layer product. It reads its
signal catalog from the companion project nbtevo-diag (Apache-2.0) and shares its decode
definitions with it by code generation (codegen/gen_dids.py), so there is a single source
of truth and no drift between the Python reader and the C collector.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project incorporates the following third-party material:

- The HMI plugin ABI header native/sdk/bmw_list.h (the bmw::* framework subset) is vendored
  verbatim from ID6_apps_prerelease
  (https://github.com/inotbarnacle/ID6_apps_prerelease), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2026 ID6 Apps contributors; the attribution is kept in that file's header.
  The native plugin shell (native/src/plugin.cpp) and collector (native/src/collector_main.c)
  are our own Apache-2.0 code written against that reconstructed ABI; the collector/plugin
  loopback-UDP split follows ID6_apps's design (documented, not copied).

The xDrive control/interlock logic in this project is an INDEPENDENT implementation and is
NOT derived from ID6_apps's controls.c (which itself derives from idrive7-apps and carries
that project's license). We deliberately keep it clean-room under Apache-2.0.

We do not incorporate nbt-aa-tile (PolyForm Noncommercial) source, nor nbt-evo-trio-collector
(no stated license) source; where their protocols are used, they are reimplemented from
documented protocol facts.
